          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Views on His Invention</strong><br>\nKalashnikov was known to have mixed feelings about his invention's global impact. He took pride in his work but was sometimes troubled by the AK-47's association with violence and conflict worldwide.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Military Influence</strong><br>\nThe legacy of Mikhail Kalashnikov is inseparable from the global recognition of the AK-47. His invention is not only a staple in military arsenals but also a cultural icon that has appeared in national flags, revolutionary imagery, and popular media.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Reflections on Kalashnikov's Life</strong><br>\nMikhail Kalashnikov died in 2013, at the age of 94. His life reflected the complexities of a man who was a patriot and a brilliant inventor, whose creation became synonymous with both national defense and guerrilla warfare. The AK-47 remains a controversial yet enduring part of his legacy.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
